1. Task_1 — Array of Objects (Employee Management System)
Write a C++ program using a class Employee to store information about 5 employees.
Each employee has:
        name
        id
        salary
The class must contain:
A function display() to display employee information.
A function isHighSalary() that returns true if the salary is greater than or equal to 1,000,000 IQD.

In main():

Create an array of 5 Employee objects.
Enter the information for the 5 employees.
Display all employees.
Display whether each employee has a high salary.
Display the employee with the highest salary.
Requirements

Students must use:
class Employee  and: Employee employees[5];

You have to use separate arrays such as:

string names[5];
int ids[5];
double salaries[5];
Expected structure
        Employee
        │
        ├── name
        ├── id
        ├── salary
        │
        ├── display()
        └── isHighSalary()
                ↓
        Employee employees[5]